   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Status of Implementation Progress: Three additional Sewage Treatment Plants with a combined capacity of 108 MLD are currently in the construction phase. Approximately 22 km of additional sewer drainpipes have been laid so far. Out of the five pumping stations, two have been completed, and work on the remaining three is in progress. A pumping main of 7.90 km has been laid so far. Furthermore, 973 additional households have been integrated into the sewerage and drainage network, although the target is set at 3,000 households.While the loan closed on 31 August 2023, ongoing spillover works are currently being funded by the state. It is anticipated that the envisioned outcome and outputs of the project design and monitoring framework will be achieved upon the successful completion of all ongoing works.</narrative>
    </title>
